-### oe calls through apm without an apm session
-
-- **Symptom:** a null read in `sdk+0x35258` (apm's session) in `oe::IsCpuOverclockEnabled`, the first call in `nnMain`; null read at `sdk+0x362b8` (`apm::SetCpuOverclockEnabled`) in the first calls of `nnMain` (`main+0x2e1e4c`); a null read (`pc=sdk+0x40720c lr=sdk+0x4071d4`) in `oe::detail::ApmSetPerformanceConfiguration` under `oe::SetPerformanceConfiguration(int)` as a movie or scene begins.
-- **Cause:** these `oe` calls go through the apm session the host never opened: `oe::IsCpuOverclockEnabled`, `oe::SetCpuOverclockEnabled(bool)`, and `oe::SetPerformanceConfiguration(int)`, the one-argument overload, which the host did not hook while it hooked `SetPerformanceConfiguration(PerformanceMode, int)`. The one-argument overload sets the configuration of both modes: in SDK 14.3 (TUNIC's `sdk+0x3a5630`) it looks the value up in a table and calls `apm::SetPerformanceConfiguration` for Normal, then for Boost; SDK 21.4.7 goes through `oe::detail::ApmSetPerformanceConfiguration`.
-- **Fix:** `hle_oe.c` hooks them; it does not scale clocks. `oe::IsCpuOverclockEnabled` reports what `SetCpuOverclockEnabled` set; both `SetPerformanceConfiguration` overloads log the value and ignore it. The import list names such calls before they are met ([Listing a game's unhooked imports before they are met](#listing-a-games-unhooked-imports-before-they-are-met)): of the builds extracted on the game drive (2026-11-15), TUNIC, FINAL FANTASY V, FINAL FANTASY VI and Overcooked import the one-argument overload as well, and no route played on them met it.
-- **Found on:** [Monster Hunter Rise](../../dm/games/0100B04011742000/README.md) (SDK 11: `IsCpuOverclockEnabled`); [Taiko Risshiden V DX](../../dm/games/0100346017304000/README.md) (SDK 12.3.3: `SetCpuOverclockEnabled`); [Warhammer Survivors](../../dm/games/0100CAA026246000/README.md) (SDK 21.4.7: `SetPerformanceConfiguration(int)`, from [PR #2318](https://github.com/seedds/nxnative/pull/2318)).
